        "intuition": "Adjusted the loss to incorporate a normalized margin scaled by the cost gap, introducing a margin term and normalizing by the sum of absolute cost gaps plus a small epsilon to prevent division by zero. This reduces direct overlap with the original function by changing the formulation and normalization, improving the gradient signals and stability. The scale is retained at 2.5 to amplify the log-prob difference signal, but the cost term now acts as a margin shift normalized per pair, ensuring the loss better reflects relative ranking quality and mitigates redundancy with the base loss.",
        "pseudocode": "margin = (cost_b - cost_a) / (abs(cost_b - cost_a) + 1e-6)\nx = alpha * scale * (lpw - lpl) - 0.1 * margin\nloss = sum(-logsigmoid(clamp(x, -20, 20)) * weight)",
